          "itemData": "{\"answerArea\": {\"calculator\": false, \"financialCalculatorMonthlyPayment\": false, \"financialCalculatorTimeToPayOff\": false, \"financialCalculatorTotalAmount\": false, \"periodicTable\": false, \"periodicTableWithKey\": false}, \"hints\": [{\"content\": \"Command of quantitative evidence questions introduce a claim that must be supported with evidence from a graph or table. This claim is usually either the hypothesis or the finding from an experiment or other research. The first thing you should do is identify the claim that you need to support. Let\\u2019s do that here: \\n\\n>**CLAIM:** The reduction in the spider population count in the enclosure with lizards by day 30 was *entirely* attributable to the presence of the lizards. \\n\\nWhat data from the table could *weaken* this conclusion?\", \"images\": {}, \"replace\": false, \"widgets\": {}}, {\"content\": \"Since we\\u2019re trying to *weaken* this conclusion, we want to show the opposite of the student\\u2019s conclusion: some of the reduction in the spider population count could be due to something other than lizards. \\n\\nWe should look for a choice that says something about the enclosure with no lizards, particularly something about a reduction in the spider population in this enclosure. \\n\\nWhich choice provides this information?\\n\", \"images\": {}, \"replace\": false, \"widgets\": {}}, {\"content\": \"(B) provides this information. It weakens the conclusion and is the answer.\", \"images\": {}, \"replace\": false, \"widgets\": {}}], \"question\": {\"content\": \"[[\\u2603 image 1]]\\n\\nTo investigate the effect of lizard predation on spider populations, a student in a biology class placed spiders in two enclosures, one with lizards and one without, and tracked the number of spiders in the enclosures for 30 days. The student concluded that the reduction in the spider population count in the enclosure with lizards by day 30 was entirely attributable to the presence of the lizards.\\n\\nWhich choice best describes data from the graph that weaken the student\\u2019s conclusion?\\n\\n[[\\u2603 radio 1]]\\n\\n\", \"images\": {}, \"widgets\": {\"image 1\": {\"alignment\": \"block\", \"graded\": true, \"options\": {\"alt\": \"Bar graph titled Spider Population Count. The horizontal axis is labeled Day of experiment. 4 data categories are shown. The vertical axis is labeled Spider count. It ranges from 0 to 90 in increments of 10.\\n\\nFor each data category, the following bars are shown:\\n\\n* no lizards\\n* with lizards\\n\\nAll values are approximate.\\nThe data for the 4 categories are as follows:\\n\\nDay 1:\\n\\n* no lizards: 85\\n* with lizards: 85\\n\\nDay 10:\\n\\n* no lizards: 62\\n* with lizards: 32\\n\\nDay 20: \\n\\n* no lizards: 51\\n* with lizards: 27\\n\\nDay 30: \\n\\n* no lizards: 43\\n* with lizards: 23\\n\", \"backgroundImage\": {\"height\": 330, \"url\": \"web+graphie://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-perseus-graphie/181769ba463dcb4a86c83bb8f5106aefbff33f28\", \"width\": 330}, \"box\": [330, 330], \"caption\": \"\", \"labels\": [], \"range\": [[0, 10], [0, 10]], \"static\": false, \"title\": \"\"}, \"static\": false, \"type\": \"image\", \"version\": {\"major\": 0, \"minor\": 0}}, \"radio 1\": {\"alignment\": \"default\", \"graded\": true, \"options\": {\"choices\": [{\"content\": \"The spider population count was the same in both enclosures on day 1.\", \"correct\": false, \"id\": \"radio-choice-0\", \"rationale\": \"This choice isn\\u2019t relevant to the claim. The claim emphasizes day *30*, not day 1. Also, this choice says nothing about the *reduction* in the spider populations. \\n\"}, {\"content\": \"The spider population count also substantially declined by day 30 in the enclosure without lizards.\", \"correct\": true, \"id\": \"radio-choice-1\", \"rationale\": \"This is the best choice. It shows that, even without lizards present, the spider population declined substantially. In other words, while lizards may cause the population to decline even more, the spiders were also dying off in the enclosure without lizards.\"}, {\"content\": \"The largest decline in spider population count in the enclosure with lizards occurred from day 1 to day 10.\", \"correct\": false, \"id\": \"radio-choice-2\", \"rationale\": \"This choice isn\\u2019t relevant to the claim. The student\\u2019s claim emphasizes *30*, not day 1. \"}, {\"content\": \"The spider population count on day 30 was lower in the enclosure with lizards than in the enclosure without lizards.\", \"correct\": false, \"id\": \"radio-choice-3\", \"rationale\": \"This choice *supports* the claim. It strengthens the association between lizards and spider population reduction, but we are looking for data to weaken the student\\u2019s claim.\"}], \"countChoices\": false, \"deselectEnabled\": false, \"hasNoneOfTheAbove\": false, \"multipleSelect\": false, \"numCorrect\": 1, \"randomize\": false}, \"static\": false, \"type\": \"radio\", \"version\": {\"major\": 3, \"minor\": 0}}}}}",
